### Sesi mendatang: Session 05 (status Mendatang, tanggal otomatis, pembicara kosong, tautan dokumentasi kosong)
- Topik: "Can AI Replace the Way We Learn?"
- Pertanyaan utama: "If AI can answer our questions, do we still need to learn by ourselves?"
- Pengantar: "AI can answer many questions in seconds. It can also write, translate, and explain. So why do we still go to school and practice? This week, let's talk about what AI can do, what it cannot do, and how we can use it wisely."
- Discussion Questions: 1) "Do you use AI to help you study?" 2) "Is getting an answer the same as understanding something?" 3) "Can AI replace the experience of learning?" 4) "What can humans do that AI cannot replace?"
- Vocabulary (7): artificial intelligence (AI) = "computer systems that can do tasks that usually need human thinking" = kecerdasan buatan = "AI can translate a sentence in one second." / depend = "to need someone or something" = bergantung = "Some students depend on AI for every homework." / understand = "to know why or how something works" = memahami = "I can copy the answer, but I want to understand it." / effort = "energy and hard work you use to do something" = usaha = "Learning takes effort." / experience = "knowledge you get from doing things" = pengalaman = "Speaking in front of the class is a good experience." / creativity = "the ability to make new ideas" = kreativitas = "Creativity helps us solve problems." / shortcut = "a faster way that skips some steps" = jalan pintas = "A shortcut is not always the best way to learn."
- Sentence starters (Express Yourself): "I think..." / "In my opinion..." / "I believe that..." / "I agree because..." / "I disagree because..." / "For example..." / "I think this is important because..."
- Mini Challenge: "Think of one opinion and two reasons to support it."
- Preparation Challenge: "Before the session, choose one question and prepare your opinion. You don't need perfect English. Just bring an idea."

### Sesi arsip (status Arsip, pembicara kosong, tautan dokumentasi kosong)
Session 04, Sabtu 21 November 2026: "Is Social Media Making Us Smarter or Distracted?"
- Pertanyaan utama: "Does social media help us learn, or does it take our attention away?"
- Ringkasan: "Students shared how videos and posts can teach new things, but also how notifications make it hard to focus. Many agreed that the way we use social media matters more than the apps themselves."
- Key Expressions: "I don't completely agree." (disagree politely; "I don't completely agree. Some videos really help me study.") / "What do you think about...?" (ask a question; "What do you think about studying with short videos?") / "From my perspective..." (give an opinion; "From my perspective, balance is the key.") / "For instance..." (give an example; "For instance, I learn new words from English channels.") / "That's an interesting point." (respond to an idea; "That's an interesting point. I never thought about that.")
- Vocabulary: distracted = "not able to focus because something else takes your attention" = terganggu / teralihkan perhatiannya = "I get distracted when my phone rings." / information = "facts or knowledge about something" = informasi = "The internet gives us a lot of information." / attention = "the act of focusing on something" = perhatian = "Please pay attention to the speaker." / balance = "a good mix, not too much of one thing" = keseimbangan = "We need a balance between study and fun." / influence = "the power to change what people think or do" = pengaruh = "Friends can have a strong influence on us."
- Speaking Challenge: "Do you think students spend too much time on social media? Give one reason or example."

Session 03, Sabtu 14 November 2026: "Why Should We Stop Being Afraid of Making Mistakes?"
- Pertanyaan utama: "What is the worst thing that can happen when we make a mistake in English?"
- Ringkasan: "Students talked about feeling embarrassed when they speak. The group agreed that mistakes show us what to improve, and that the audience usually cares more about the idea than the grammar."
- Key Expressions: "I have a different opinion." (disagree politely; "I have a different opinion. I think mistakes are useful.") / "Why do you think so?" (ask for a reason; "Why do you think so? Can you explain?") / "Could you explain that?" (ask for clarification; "Could you explain that again, please?") / "This is because..." (give a reason; "This is because we learn from our mistakes.") / "I think you're right because..." (agree; "I think you're right because practice makes us braver.")
- Vocabulary: mistake = "something that is not correct" = kesalahan = "Everyone makes mistakes." / afraid = "feeling fear" = takut = "I was afraid to speak at first." / brave = "ready to do something difficult" = berani = "She was brave to try." / embarrassed = "feeling shy or uncomfortable in front of others" = malu = "I felt embarrassed when I forgot the word." / improve = "to become better" = meningkat / memperbaiki = "We improve when we practice."
- Speaking Challenge: "Share a time you made a mistake and what you learned from it."

Session 02, Sabtu 7 November 2026: "Why Is Practice More Important Than Memorization?"
- Pertanyaan utama: "Is it better to remember many words or to use a few words every day?"
- Ringkasan: "Students compared memorizing word lists with using words in real conversations. The group concluded that words we use often stay in our memory longer than words we only copy."
- Key Expressions: "What I mean is..." (clarify; "What I mean is we should use the words, not only read them.") / "In other words..." (restate; "In other words, practice makes it easier.") / "I agree with you because..." (agree; "I agree with you because speaking builds confidence.") / "Let me give you an example." (give an example; "Let me give you an example. I learned 'proud' when I used it in a sentence.") / "To sum up..." (conclude; "To sum up, practice is better than only memorizing.")
- Vocabulary: practice = "to do something again and again to get better" = berlatih / latihan = "We practice speaking every Saturday." / memorize = "to learn something so you can remember it exactly" = menghafal = "I memorize ten words, but I forget them." / habit = "something you do regularly" = kebiasaan = "Speaking English can be a good habit." / repeat = "to say or do something again" = mengulang = "Please repeat the question." / improve = "to become better" = meningkat / memperbaiki = "Daily practice helps us improve."
- Speaking Challenge: "What is one English habit you can do every day? Explain why."

Session 01, Sabtu 31 Oktober 2026: "Why Is English Important for Our Future?"
- Pertanyaan utama: "How can English open doors for our future?"
- Ringkasan: "Students shared how English helps with school, technology, travel, and future jobs. They agreed that small daily practice matters more than perfect grammar."
- Key Expressions: "In my opinion..." (give an opinion; "In my opinion, English helps us find better jobs.") / "One reason is..." (give a reason; "One reason is that many websites are in English.") / "For example..." (give an example; "For example, I watch videos in English to learn.") / "I see your point, but..." (disagree politely; "I see your point, but we also need our own language.") / "That's why I think..." (conclude; "That's why I think English is important.")
- Vocabulary: future = "the time that will come after now" = masa depan = "English can help my future." / opportunity = "a chance to do something good" = kesempatan = "Speaking club is a good opportunity." / communicate = "to share ideas or information with others" = berkomunikasi = "We communicate with people around the world." / global = "related to the whole world" = global / mendunia = "English is a global language." / confident = "sure about yourself" = percaya diri = "I feel more confident now."
- Speaking Challenge: "Tell us one way English can help you in ten years."

### Speaking Toolkit awal (8 kategori; tiap ekspresi diberi arti Indonesia yang akurat dan satu contoh kalimat sederhana oleh Anda)
1. Giving Opinions: "I think..." / "In my opinion..." / "I believe..."
2. Agreeing: "I agree with you." / "That's true." / "I think you're right because..."
3. Disagreeing Politely: "I don't completely agree." / "I see your point, but..." / "I have a different opinion."
4. Giving Reasons: "This is because..." / "One reason is..." / "The main reason is..."
5. Giving Examples: "For example..." / "For instance..." / "Let me give you an example."
6. Asking Questions: "What do you think about...?" / "Why do you think so?" / "Could you explain that?"
7. Clarifying Ideas: "What I mean is..." / "Let me explain." / "In other words..."
8. Concluding: "To sum up..." / "In conclusion..." / "That's why I think..."

